==Trivia==
*''Doron'' (どろん) is the Japanese onomatopoeia for a person or creature vanishing, such as a ninja concealing themselves with a smoke screen. The closest in English would be "poof". In this case, it literally refers to how Elder Flame Doron disappears for good after attacking.
*His Japanese name, 古神炎ドロン ''Ko Kamien Doron'', may contain a subtle pun: 神炎 ''kamien'' ("god-flame") sounds almost like 仮面 ''kamen'' (mask).
*When unmasked, he looks fairly similar to a [[mariowiki:Boo|Boo]] from the ''Mario'' franchise.
*He is currently the only [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemy who doesn't inflict the curse effect.
*He and [[Wafer Cat XL (Enemy)]] are the only enemies to have the self-destructive ability.
**He is currently the only self-destructive enemy to appear outside of [[Event Stages]].
*He is the first non-stationary enemy to be immune to Surges.
*He is tied with [[Summerluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Fabulous Pasalan]] for the highest Surge level and is tied with [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Freshman Cat Jobs]] and the [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou|PC exclusive]] unit [[Natsu Mikan (PC Uber Rare Cat)|Natsu Mikan]] for the strongest weaken of any character in the game, reducing unit damage to 1% of what it was originally.
*In the sub-chapter preview for [[Ancient Forest Labyrinth]] and [[Humanity Catified]], his icon is replaced with an image error icon. This was later fixed in [[Version 12.6 Update|Version 12.6]].
*He is tied with [[EVA Unit-13 (Enemy)|EVA Unit-13]] for the enemy with the highest number of [[Special Abilities]] at 10.

